# Forward Hyprland's socket2 events, one line per event, as a listener.
# A listener must follow its input declarations directly, so the caller composes
# the socat address from the session environment:
#   XDG_RUNTIME_DIR              the user's runtime directory
#   HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE  the running compositor's instance name
# The socket is $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hypr/$HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE/.socket2.sock.
# Each record is the handler's pipeline input and is forwarded unchanged.
# Run from a Hyprland session with:
#   execute examples/desktop/hyprland-events.program --input address="UNIX-CONNECT:$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hypr/$HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE/.socket2.sock"
accept address as text

listen to hypr.socket2 with address address
whenever a line arrives as event
  then "cat"
